The public availability of this project, including availability through repositories, websites, or platforms such as Steam Workshop or Git hosting services, does not create any implied permission to reuse, modify, distribute, or create derivative works.

3. Definitions

3.1 Project

"Project" refers to this software project, including its source code, scripts, assets, documentation, examples, configuration files, and other materials distributed by the copyright holder.

3.2 Derivative Work

"Derivative Work" means any work based upon, adapted from, modified from, translated from, ported from, or incorporating substantial portions of the protected expression contained within this project.

Examples include:

- Modified versions of this project.
- Forks or alternative distributions.
- Ports to other games, platforms, or engines.
- Projects incorporating substantial portions of this project's source code or implementation.
- Recreated versions that reuse protected source material.

3.3 Public API

A "Public API" means only functions, events, hooks, interfaces, or integration points explicitly designated in writing by the copyright holder as Public API.

Public visibility within source code does not automatically make a component part of the Public API.

